# {{project_name}}

A descending-price Dutch auction contract, generated by
[soroban-forge](https://github.com/soroban-forge-labs/soroban-forge) from the
`dutch-auction` template.

## How it works

A Dutch auction sells an asset where the price starts at `start_price` and
linearly decays to a `floor_price` over a configured `duration_seconds`:

1. **Initialization & Funding** — The seller initializes the auction parameters
   (`asset_token`, `payment_token`, `asset_amount`, `start_price`, `floor_price`,
   `duration_seconds`) and calls `fund` to deposit the asset into escrow.
2. **Linear price decay** — Price decays linearly over time:
   $$\text{price}(t) = \text{start\_price} - \frac{(\text{start\_price} - \text{floor\_price}) \times \text{elapsed}}{\text{duration}}$$
   Before the start time, price is `start_price`. After the duration ends, price
   remains at `floor_price`.
3. **Immediate settlement** — The first buyer to call `buy` purchases the asset
   at the current price. Payment is transferred to the seller, the asset is
   transferred to the buyer, and the auction settles.
4. **Cancel** — If no buyer has purchased yet, the seller can cancel the
   auction and reclaim their asset.

## Develop

```sh
cargo test                 # run unit tests
stellar contract build     # build the deployable wasm
```

## Deploy to testnet

```sh
stellar contract deploy \
  --wasm target/wasm32v1-none/release/{{crate_name}}.wasm \
  --source-account <your-identity> \
  --network testnet
```

Then initialize and fund:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <SELLER> \
  --network testnet \
  -- initialize \
  --seller <SELLER_ADDRESS> \
  --asset_token <ASSET_TOKEN_ADDRESS> \
  --payment_token <PAYMENT_TOKEN_ADDRESS> \
  --asset_amount 1000 \
  --start_price 10000 \
  --floor_price 2000 \
  --duration_seconds 86400

stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <SELLER> \
  --network testnet \
  -- fund
```

Query the current price:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <ANY_ADDRESS> \
  --network testnet \
  -- get_current_price
```

A buyer purchases the asset:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <BUYER> \
  --network testnet \
  -- buy \
  --buyer <BUYER_ADDRESS>
```

